          "deepDive": "**〜に限らず** is the negative of 〜に限る (*to be limited to*): *not limited to ~* → *not only ~ (but others too)*. It **widens** the scope: the noun before it is one example, and the second half usually says the same holds for others, often with **も / でも / どんな〜でも / あらゆる〜**.\n\n- 夏に限らず、年間を通して… (*not just in summer but all year round*)\n- アメリカに限らず、ヨーロッパでも… (*not only in America but also in Europe*)\n\nIt attaches directly to a noun. For verbs and adjectives use 〜のみならず (#63) or 〜だけでなく.\n\nDistinguish it from look-alikes (the practice pits these against each other):\n- **〜を問わず** (#2): *regardless of* — needs a noun with a range of values or a pair (年齢を問わず, 男女を問わず). 人間を問わず is wrong because 人間 doesn't express a range.\n- **〜にもかかわらず** (#21): *despite ~* — a completely different meaning (concession): すぐ近くにもかかわらず1時間もかかった.\n- **〜において** (#6): *in / at (a field)* — just a location marker.\n- **〜にしたがって** (#65): proportional change.\n\nAnd other members of the 限る family (☞ p.223 〜に限る／限り): **Nに限り** (#3, *only N*), **Nに限って〜ない** (#3, *N of all people would never*), **Vかぎり** (#23, *as long as*), **Nに限って** (#86, *just when / of all times*), **〜に限る** (#104, *~ is best*). Notice the neat opposition: 会員に限り (only members) vs. 会員に限らず (not only members).\n\nJLPT tip: if the second half contains も or でも and adds more members to the group, に限らず is likely correct.",
